Q: Equal height divs - complicated with multiple backgrounds A: <p>Save yourself the trouble and just use tables for the outer layout.  They just work.</p>

<p>Here's the table example:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd"&gt;
&lt;html&gt;

&lt;head&gt;
&lt;title&gt;left&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
        .side { background-color:blue;color:white;width:235px;vertical-align:top;margin:0px;padding:0px;}
        .left3 {padding:0px 0px 0px 17px;vertical-align:top;}
        .mainContent {margin:0px;vertical-align:top;}
        table {width:100%;height:100%;border-collapse:collapse;}
        html,body{width:100%;height:100%;margin:0px;}
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
    &lt;tr&gt;
        &lt;td class="side"&gt;left
            &lt;table&gt;
                &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="side"&gt;left side 2
                    &lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="left3"&gt;Left Side 3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
                &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
            &lt;/table&gt;
        &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td class="mainContent"&gt;center&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;td class="side"&gt;right&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>

